Lilak, Persian Spell Checking Dictionary
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/lexicon/fa-stems.bin is derived from the Lilak fa-IR dictionary.

    Copyright 2015 Mostafa Sedaghat Joo
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
    https://github.com/b00f/lilak

The derived artifact contains the dictionary's stem list, normalized to the
canonical Persian form used throughout this project, deduplicated, sorted and
front-coded. Affix rules are not applied. No modification of meaning is made.

Obtained via the npm package `dictionary-fa@2.0.0`, which redistributes the
same dictionary under the same license. See data/provenance/lexicon.json for
the upstream SHA-256 and byte counts.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deliberate exclusions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following widely used Persian resources are NOT included, because their
licensing is incompatible with an MIT-licensed package. They are listed here
so the exclusion is a recorded decision rather than an oversight:

  * Hazm `words.dat` — the repository is MIT, but its annotations derive from
    the Peykare/Bijankhan corpus, which is research/non-commercial.
  * `behnam/persian-words-frequency` — CC BY-SA 3.0. ShareAlike would infect a
    shipped frequency table, which is exactly the artifact it would apply to.
  * Virastyar, perstem, PersianStemmer, Vajehdan — GPL/AGPL.
  * Several large GitHub word lists (240k/494k/700k entries) — no license file.
  * `Arshia82sbn/Finglish-To-Persian-Dataset-Large` — tagged Apache-2.0, but
    built in part from GPLv3 Virastyar rules over a corpus with no stated
    provenance.

See docs/open-items.md for the full survey.
